\section*{Week 15: XCM \& Integration Summary}

\subsection*{Planned Deliverables (from thesis plan)}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Implement cross-chain message handlers and parachain transfers
    \item Integrate Ethereum bridge
    \item Develop chain extensions for efficiency
    \item Test initial integrations
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{What Was Built}

\subsubsection*{1. XCM Cross-Chain Extrinsics}

\textbf{Location:} pallets/content-rights/src/lib.rs

Cross-chain operations implemented as pallet extrinsics that construct and send XCM messages:

\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\caption{XCM Cross-Chain Extrinsics}
{\footnotesize
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{lLL}
\toprule
\textbf{Operation} & \textbf{Extrinsic} & \textbf{XCM Flow} \\
\midrule
Cross-chain subscription renewal & renew\_subscription\_cross\_chain & Source parachain $\rightarrow$ Target parachain via WithdrawAsset + BuyExecution + Transact \\
Cross-chain PPV access & pay\_per\_view\_cross\_chain & Same pattern as renewal \\
Cross-chain ownership transfer & transfer\_ownership\_cross\_chain & Source $\rightarrow$ Target with ownership state update \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
}
\end{table}

\textbf{XCM config changes} (runtime/src/configs/xcm\_config.rs):
\begin{itemize}
    \item RelayNetwork set to Some(NetworkId::ByGenesis(ROCOCO\_GENESIS\_HASH))
    \item UniversalLocation includes GlobalConsensus for absolute location resolution
    \item LocationToAccountId extended with HashedDescription, GlobalConsensusParachainConvertsFor for Ethereum origins
    \item Paid execution barriers (WithdrawAsset + BuyExecution, not UnpaidExecution)
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Relevant commits:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item 9d88646 --- Add XCM cross-chain extrinsics for content rights operations
    \item 25265ee --- Add Snowbridge XCM config (Ethereum origin converters, GlobalConsensus)
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection*{2. Ethereum Bridge Integration (Snowbridge)}

Full local Snowbridge v1 bridge setup connecting Ethereum to the Content Rights parachain:

\textbf{Infrastructure:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item 4-chain Zombienet topology (Relay, Bridge Hub 1013, AssetHub 1000, Content Rights 100)
    \item Geth v1.17.1 (Ethereum execution layer)
    \item Lodestar v1.35.0 (Ethereum consensus/beacon layer, mainnet preset)
    \item 16 Gateway contracts deployed on Ethereum via Forge
    \item Beacon light client initialized on Bridge Hub
    \item Beacon relay + Ethereum relay running
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Key scripts:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item scripts/snowbridge-full-setup.sh --- Automated end-to-end Ethereum side setup
    \item scripts/open-hrmp-snowbridge.mjs --- HRMP channel setup for 4-chain topology
    \item scripts/configure-snowbridge.mjs --- Substrate-side Snowbridge configuration
    \item scripts/deploy-gateway.sh --- Contract deployment + BEEFY checkpoint
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Relevant commits:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item 25265ee --- Snowbridge local bridge setup
    \item 7b967d8 --- Automated full setup script
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Documentation:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item docs/SNOWBRIDGE\_SETUP.md --- Setup plan (7 phases)
    \item docs/SNOWBRIDGE\_SESSION\_LOG.md --- Detailed session log with lessons learned
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection*{3. Chain Extensions / Precompiles}

Instead of traditional chain extensions, a \textbf{custom pallet-revive precompile} was implemented for efficient contract-to-pallet calls:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Precompile address: 0x0000...0400
    \item Function: check\_access(content\_id, account) --- returns access status
    \item Allows ink! contracts to query pallet state without cross-contract calls
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Relevant commit:} 7bc9651

\subsubsection*{4. Cross-Chain Storage Proof Verification}

\textbf{Location:} pallets/rights-verifier/

pallet-rights-verifier enables trustless cross-chain verification of content rights by verifying Merkle storage proofs from remote parachains:

\begin{itemize}
    \item verify\_rights\_proof --- Verifies a storage proof against a relay chain state root
    \item Enables a parachain to confirm subscription/ownership status on another parachain without XCM round-trips
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Relevant commit:} 696d990

